+# Editor acceptance after HB-20
+
+HB-19 and HB-20 close the named editor presentation/RTL V leaves. Their
+[chrome receipt](editor-chrome-presentation/results.json) and
+[rich editor receipt](rich-editor-presentation/results.json) retain scope and
+rendered-review limits. Earlier wave-03 statements that these twenty V leaves
+remain open are historical. Do not reassign or rerun those reviews for credit.
+
+Wave-03 command/image/runtime proposals are integrated. The
+[followup receipt](wave-03-followup/validation-results.json) records native
+selection restoration and ordinary editing fixes; the integrated command suite
+covers partial-run case/clear, Unicode expansion, six alignments, colors and
+history/reload. Native Uppercase/Clear and Cancel/Apply/lifetime cases passed in
+all three engines. Preserve original failures and the focused correction history.
+
+The [wave-04 editor reconciliation](wave-04/02/results.json) recommends A-M-26,
+A-M-28 and A-M-30 complete for coordinator review. It preserves all twelve original
+obligations verbatim and records evidence hashes. It does not edit central counts.
+Typeface selection belongs to RichTextFormattingToolbar; TextStyleMenuControl
+retains its eight owned style commands.
+
+Remaining acceptance is bounded by these concrete decisions/results:
+
+| IDs | Next deliverable |
+| --- | --- |
+| A-M-27 | Reconcile one actual successful insertion result announcement and editor focus in its host. Callback status text alone does not prove spoken output. |
+| A-M-29 | Keyboard/AT operation of actual OS color chooser in both modes: focus, confirm/cancel, callback and return focus. Hex-input automation is separate evidence. |
+| A-M-34, A-E-02 | Owner-supported saved-document/node/version corpus and malformed/unknown input recovery policy; add only missing approved edit/reload/read-only cases. Preserve the original on rejection/partial parsing. |
+| A-E-03 | Successful Image/Columns insertion at same-node/cross-node ranges where missing, with rich-run/paragraph, selection/focus and undo/reload outcomes. Existing Cancel/Link Apply rows remain accepted. |
+| A-E-04 | Current consumer list/code/table transformation and selection requirements, compared against existing cases before adding gaps. |
+| A-E-05 | Actual configured OS IME conversion/commit/cancel in editor/title/color; named device/browser/AT traversal, state, focus and clipboard observations. |
+| A-E-06 | Native malformed-metadata retry proposal and real host upload byte/type/size/dimension/authorization/abort/stale-asset cleanup evidence. |
+| A-E-07 | Owner CSS/resource, unknown-schema/recovery and downstream-renderer decisions, followed by native hostile-content request/geometry checks against that policy. |
+
+The [two-file retry patch](wave-04/02/metadata-retry.patch) extends the existing
+image-source host/test rather than adding another fixture or duplicate suite.
+Its three attempts reject an unsafe address, reject malformed metadata on a safe
+address, then accept valid metadata. The file/description and saved content remain
+intact through both rejected attempts. The [bounded plan](wave-04/02/validation-plan.json)
+is executable after coordinator integration; no new native pass is claimed yet.
+
+For host decisions, supply representative saved documents and exact versions;
+name required transformations and selection shapes; state reject/migrate/recover
+behavior; identify accepted resource origins/redirects/data/blob rules and allowed
+CSS; and provide upload adapter outcomes for cancellation and stale assets.
+The UI cannot infer asset authorization or delete host assets. Keep raw rejected
+URL/JSON fidelity distinct from safe rendering; downstream consumers validate
+their own HTML, style and URL contexts.
+
+Reuse [the existing operator protocol](wave-03-25/operator-validation.md) and
+[trust decision review](wave-03-26/trust-review.md). DOM/axe results and authored
+protocols are not spoken AT, actual IME or service execution. The existing simulator
+VoiceOver selector smoke is scoped to its selector case. Future packaging/features,
+legal approval and production release gates remain separate.
